       "text": "I haven't entered this order. 50 mg is five times the maximum recommended daily dose of amlodipine for adults, which is 10 mg once daily. At that dose there is a serious risk of profound hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and prolonged vasodilatory shock. Amlodipine's half-life is long, 30 to 50 hours, so the effects could last a long time and be hard to reverse.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **5 mg** by mouth once daily, the usual starting dose\n- **10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum dose\n- Another dose, such as 2.5 mg for a frail patient or one who needs a gentler start\n\nIf 50 mg is what you want, please confirm that explicitly and tell me the clinical reason. I can then enter it with a note documenting that it was intentional. Otherwise, give me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
